1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,994
You don't need to know how to code.

2
00:00:02,994 --> 00:00:06,504
You just need to say clearly what you
want. In this unit,

3
00:00:06,504 --> 00:00:11,143
we use Google Antigravity and its built-in
AI Agent to go all the way from

4
00:00:11,143 --> 00:00:13,462
installation to a playable mini-game.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,883
There are four parts: install and set up,
ask the AI to install tools,

6
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:23,685
build a first web page as a warm-up, and
finally build a Memory Match game.

7
00:00:23,685 --> 00:00:29,128
Classroom computers are already set up, so
you can start right at checking the tools.

8
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:34,059
On your own computer, go to the official
download page.

9
00:00:34,059 --> 00:00:37,398
Careful: don't pick the app or CLI at the
top.

10
00:00:37,398 --> 00:00:40,447
Scroll down to Antigravity IDE Standalone.

11
00:00:40,447 --> 00:00:45,310
On Windows, most people choose x64; on a
Mac, choose Apple Silicon.

12
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:48,900
Open it and sign in with your Google
account.

13
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,796
The built-in AI Agent is right there on
the right:

14
00:00:51,796 --> 00:00:54,634
nothing extra to install, and no API key
needed.

15
00:00:54,634 --> 00:00:57,266
If your work or school account is
restricted,

16
00:00:57,266 --> 00:00:59,431
use a personal Gmail account instead.

17
00:01:00,367 --> 00:01:02,891
The AI only works inside the folder you
open.

18
00:01:02,891 --> 00:01:06,986
So for every project, create a new folder
and select it with Open Folder.

19
00:01:06,986 --> 00:01:11,138
In the bottom right, you can also choose
the model and the thinking level.

20
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,422
Want more AI Agents?

21
00:01:13,422 --> 00:01:14,942
Add them as extensions.

22
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:20,162
In Extensions on the left, search for
Claude Code and Codex, and click Install.

23
00:01:20,162 --> 00:01:22,013
Then go to View, Appearance,

24
00:01:22,013 --> 00:01:25,383
and set Secondary Activity Bar Position to
Default.

25
00:01:25,383 --> 00:01:29,679
An icon for each agent appears on the
right; click one to switch.

26
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:34,372
In the same editor, you can switch agents
and switch models.

27
00:01:34,372 --> 00:01:37,642
Claude Code offers models such as Opus 5.5
and Sonnet

28
00:01:37,642 --> 00:01:40,541
5.5; Codex offers GPT-5.6 Sol, Terra and
Luna;

29
00:01:40,541 --> 00:01:45,152
and the built-in Antigravity Agent offers
models such as Gemini 3.8 Flash.

30
00:01:45,152 --> 00:01:50,137
Note that Claude Code and Codex each need
you to sign in with their own account.

31
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:51,935
Now the panels.

32
00:01:51,935 --> 00:01:56,275
On the left is the Explorer; click a file
and its contents open in the middle.

33
00:01:56,275 --> 00:01:58,668
On the right is where you chat with the
AI,

34
00:01:58,668 --> 00:02:01,228
and below the input box you can switch
models.

35
00:02:01,228 --> 00:02:05,234
If you installed Claude Code, you can
switch to it on the right as well.

36
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,514
Next, ask the AI to install tools.

37
00:02:08,514 --> 00:02:13,209
One sentence is enough: it detects your
operating system, checks Git,

38
00:02:13,209 --> 00:02:18,040
uv and Node.js, installs only what's
missing, and reports the versions.

39
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,776
Then the second prompt: ask the AI to
install GitHub CLI,

40
00:02:22,776 --> 00:02:24,300
LibreOffice and ffmpeg.

41
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:28,474
Again, it skips what's installed, explains
anything that fails,

42
00:02:28,474 --> 00:02:29,998
and lists the versions.

43
00:02:29,998 --> 00:02:33,311
When it wants to run a command, just click
Accept.

44
00:02:33,311 --> 00:02:36,623
After installing, remember to restart
Antigravity.

45
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:38,637
A quick warm-up:

46
00:02:38,637 --> 00:02:43,785
ask the AI to create hello.html showing
Hello Antigravity and today's date in

47
00:02:43,785 --> 00:02:46,459
large text, then open it in the browser.

48
00:02:46,459 --> 00:02:51,741
If you see the page, the AI can create
files and run commands on your computer.

49
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,846
The main example is Memory Match.

50
00:02:54,846 --> 00:02:59,397
A good prompt makes four things clear: use
Vite and JS; sixteen cards,

51
00:02:59,397 --> 00:03:03,039
matching pairs disappear, with a move
count and a timer;

52
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:06,160
show Congratulations when every card is
cleared;

53
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:09,021
and start the web page as soon as it's
done.

54
00:03:09,967 --> 00:03:12,998
The AI creates the project, installs the
packages,

55
00:03:12,998 --> 00:03:16,513
starts a development server and gives you
a localhost URL.

56
00:03:16,513 --> 00:03:19,330
Open it and play a round: if flipping, the
move

57
00:03:19,330 --> 00:03:21,908
count and the timer all work, you're done.

58
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:24,367
Want to change something?

59
00:03:24,367 --> 00:03:27,274
Just tell it in one sentence: turn the
cards into

60
00:03:27,274 --> 00:03:29,885
fruit, add a best record, use twenty
cards.

61
00:03:29,885 --> 00:03:31,985
Refresh the page to see the change.

62
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:35,727
When something goes wrong, there's one
universal fix:

63
00:03:35,727 --> 00:03:37,835
paste the whole error message to the AI.

64
00:03:37,835 --> 00:03:41,683
You can also send a screenshot of the
error or the part that looks wrong,

65
00:03:41,683 --> 00:03:43,844
and let the AI find the cause and fix it.

66
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,746
One folder and one clear sentence,

67
00:03:46,746 --> 00:03:49,722
and the AI can build a working project
from scratch.

68
00:03:49,722 --> 00:03:53,785
Keep this game: in the next unit, we
install the frontend-design skill,

69
00:03:53,785 --> 00:03:55,387
build it again, and compare.

